From 2e9ceeff4141509693f05e4ac3b769cbc5ebf3e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:02:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 186/191] Review fixes: scanout layout, native map split,
 64-bit CD reads, EINTR, helper threads off pinned cores

- gs_pgs readback: the scanout image goes back to READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL after its copy (a full-colour frame shown on
  two vsyncs is the same image; the second barrier declared a layout it no longer had).
- ga2_nativemap: a frame that is not the battle map clears "ready", so the desktop's Fast map stops splitting the
  picture into scene and UI layer after a battle.
- readHostRange (EE-side sceCdRead stubs): positional 64-bit reads (ga2_fileread) instead of ifstream::seekg,
  which stops at 2 GiB on Windows.
- ga2_fileread: pread retried on EINTR.
- ga2_affinity: the process's CPU mask saved before the game thread is pinned (big.LITTLE); the sharp-text worker,
  the flat-art redraw worker and the Anime4K cache writer give themselves the original mask back.

From the 0.12.0 code review (research/review-0.12/review.md). Verified: unit tests 661/662 (the known VU0 table
check); desktop runs of the Eigou 1 battle and story.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
